  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>The second of Selvedge e&#39;s large moons, an ice shell over a brine ocean about seventy kilometres down, kept warm by tidal flexing in a three-body resonance. Its vent communities are the best characterised in the galaxy, because the ice is thin at the leading pole and a bore reached water in a single season. The surface is fissured, sulphur-stained along the fractures, and very quiet.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
